00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:50.630
Now, before we get into it, remember that
a pardon is a form of clemency.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:55.700
A pardon is when a government official forgives
a certain criminal offense.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.800
The offense, uh, can stay on the person's
criminal record.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.179
The person is not subject to further restrictions
or criminal penalties that other convicts

00:01:06.179 --> 00:01:08.759
or ex-convicts may be subjected to.

00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:11.580
A pardon is a form of clemency.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:17.459
Clemency is a general term for reducing the
penalty for a particular crime without clearing

00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:18.459
the criminal record.

00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:22.799
It could be a pardon, could be that a sentence
gets commuted, could be a reprieve, which

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:27.200
is you temporarily put off or suspend the
punishment, but don't cancel it all together.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.200
In total.

